From 47fba99d27015dd74a164962b7952a0e1c8df6f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 15:20:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Two conventional window frames: Prose and Prose Right

A full-width title bar sized from the system font, a thin frame of the same
colour, a one-pixel outline, and the buttons at one end: round close,
minimize and zoom at the left with the title centred (Prose), or minimize,
zoom and close glyphs at the right with the title at the left (Prose
Right). Every colour is a system window colour, so Appearance -- or a
theme -- restyles them without a rebuild.

Built on SATDecorator, so stack-and-tile highlighting and the standard
window behaviour are unchanged; only the tab model is replaced by a bar.
Stacked windows share the bar as equal slices, each with its own close
button, which the Mac and Win decorators in the tree never did. Modal
windows keep Haiku's frame-only look; document windows keep their knob.

Haiku's own decorator add-ons live in haiku_extras, which this image has
never shipped, so these go into the system package. Verified in a guest:
switched to live with setdecor, the close button closes, all three looks
draw, focus states draw.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
